  "notes": "USAGE:\nA formal suru verb ({樹立|じゅりつ}する). Most commonly used for setting records ({記録|きろく}を{樹立|じゅりつ}する) or establishing formal relations or systems. The kanji {樹|じゅ} (tree) conveys the metaphor of planting something that will stand firm.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {記録|きろく}を{樹立|じゅりつ}する: to set a record\n- {世界|せかい}{記録|きろく}を{樹立|じゅりつ}する: to set a world record\n- {外交|がいこう}{関係|かんけい}を{樹立|じゅりつ}する: to establish diplomatic relations\n- {政権|せいけん}を{樹立|じゅりつ}する: to establish a government",
